# Referral bonus rules

This file implements the plain English referral bonus specification.

> Module Reencoded2

## Facts supplied and values to determine

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ReferralBonus:
  # Facts supplied
  input grade content integer
  input is_hard_to_fill content boolean
  input agency_introduced content boolean
  input agency_introduction_date content date
  input referral_date content date
  input first_day_of_employment content date
  input has_ceased content boolean
  input cessation_date content date
  input cessation_by_redundancy content boolean
  input bonus_already_paid_this_year content money

  # Values to determine
  output qualifying_period_end content date
  output entitlement content money
  output payable content boolean
  output bonus_before_cap content money
  output bonus_payable content money
```

## The qualifying period

The qualifying period is 180 days beginning on the referred person's first day
of employment. The first day is day 1, so the period ends on the 179th day
after it.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  # Advancing a date by 12 months onto a day that does not exist rounds down
  # to the last day of the month.
  date round down

  label qualifying_period definition qualifying_period_end equals
    first_day_of_employment + 179 day
```

## Rules for the entitlement

The hierarchy runs, from most general to most specific: the standard rule, then
the senior-grade rule, then the hard-to-fill rule, then the agency rule, then
the stale-agency rule. Each is an exception to the one before it. Each rule
states its own condition in full.

### Standard rule

By default the entitlement is 1,000.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label standard_rule definition entitlement equals $1,000.00
```

### Senior-grade rule

As an exception to the standard rule: where the grade is 5 or more, the
entitlement is 2,500.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label senior_grade_rule exception standard_rule
  definition entitlement
    under condition grade >= 5
    consequence equals $2,500.00
```

### Hard-to-fill rule

As an exception to the senior-grade rule: where the role is hard-to-fill, the
entitlement is 4,000.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label hard_to_fill_rule exception senior_grade_rule
  definition entitlement
    under condition is_hard_to_fill
    consequence equals $4,000.00
```

### Agency rule

As an exception to the hard-to-fill rule: where an agency introduced the
candidate AND that introduction happened strictly before the referral was
submitted, the entitlement is nil.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label agency_rule exception hard_to_fill_rule
  definition entitlement
    under condition
      agency_introduced and agency_introduction_date < referral_date
    consequence equals $0.00
```

### Stale-agency rule

As an exception to the agency rule: where an agency introduced the candidate,
that introduction happened strictly before the referral was submitted, AND the
introduction was more than 12 months before the referral, the entitlement is
re-derived as it would have been under the standard, senior-grade and
hard-to-fill rules.

"More than 12 months before" means the introduction date advanced by 12 months
is strictly earlier than the referral date.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label stale_agency_rule exception agency_rule
  definition entitlement
    under condition
      agency_introduced
      and agency_introduction_date < referral_date
      and agency_introduction_date + 12 month < referral_date
    consequence equals
      if is_hard_to_fill then $4,000.00
      else if grade >= 5 then $2,500.00
      else $1,000.00
```

## Rules for payability

### Payable rule

By default the bonus is payable.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label payable_rule definition payable equals true
```

### Early-cessation rule

As an exception to the payable rule: where the referred person has ceased
employment and the cessation date is on or before the last day of the
qualifying period, the bonus is not payable.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label early_cessation_rule exception payable_rule
  definition payable
    under condition
      has_ceased and cessation_date <= qualifying_period_end
    consequence equals false
```

### Redundancy rule

As an exception to the early-cessation rule: where the referred person has
ceased employment on or before the last day of the qualifying period AND the
cessation was by reason of redundancy, the bonus is payable.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label redundancy_rule exception early_cessation_rule
  definition payable
    under condition
      has_ceased
      and cessation_date <= qualifying_period_end
      and cessation_by_redundancy
    consequence equals true
```

## Combining entitlement and payability

`bonus_before_cap` is the entitlement where the bonus is payable, and nil
otherwise. There is no exception to this.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label combination definition bonus_before_cap equals
    if payable then entitlement else $0.00
```

## The annual limit

The total payable to a worker in any financial year must not exceed 10,000, and
that limit is applied after everything above.

```catala
scope ReferralBonus:
  label annual_limit definition bonus_payable equals
    if $10,000.00 - bonus_already_paid_this_year <= $0.00 then $0.00
    else if bonus_before_cap > $10,000.00 - bonus_already_paid_this_year then
      $10,000.00 - bonus_already_paid_this_year
    else bonus_before_cap
```
